# Build context pruning. This file applies to TWO different builds, and the
# exclusions below must be safe for both:
#
#   1. The SDK image, which takes core/ as a BuildKit NAMED context:
#
#          docker build --build-context core=../core -f sdk/dockerfiles/Dockerfile sdk/
#
#   2. The external test image, for which core/ IS the build context directly
#      (see the external-test-docker target in core/Makefile):
#
#          docker build -t silex-test -f tests/external/Dockerfile .
#
# The weight is entirely tests/external/repos -- vendored checkouts of oil,
# cpython, coreutils, grep and friends, 1.4 GB of the 1.4 GB that tests/ costs.
# Everything else under tests/ is 752 KB.
#
# So exclude the repos, NOT all of tests/. Excluding tests/ wholesale prunes
# tests/external/docker-run.sh out of build (2), whose Dockerfile then does
# `COPY . .` and produces an image missing the very script the Makefile asks it
# to run -- `bash: tests/external/docker-run.sh: No such file or directory`,
# exit 127, before a single suite executes. The build cost of keeping the rest
# of tests/ is under a megabyte.
tests/external/repos/
# build/ is safe to prune for both: docker-run.sh runs `make clean` and
# `make release-glibc` inside the container rather than using a host build.
build/
*.gcov

# Nothing below is needed to compile the binary.
docs/
*.md
.git/
.github/
